        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "04a62496-2af6-588e-8c69-f8993a42ad62",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Minardi M190, Minardi M189B, Cosworth DFR V8 engine, Pirelli tyres\n- Companies: Pirelli & C. S.p.A., ChemChina, Pirelli North America, Bohn Aluminum, Wicks, Lowe's\n- People: James Edward Arnold\n- Places: Milan, Italy\n\nFacts:\n- Pirelli & C. S.p.A. was listed on the Milan Stock Exchange starting in 1922.\n- Pirelli & C. S.p.A. is a multinational company based in Milan, Italy, and it is now an overseas subsidiary of the Chinese state-owned enterprise ChemChina.\n- The Minardi M189 was updated as the Minardi M189B for the season and was used for the first two races of the year before being replaced by the Minardi M190.\n- The Minardi M190 was powered by the Cosworth DFR V8 engine and ran on Pirelli tyres.\n- James Edward Arnold was one of the last presidents of Pirelli North America, and he was also president of Bohn Aluminum and a major consultant to Wicks, which was known for owning the Lowe's hardware chain.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
